shader: shadow the data registers of RED and SURED

From Lichii PR 149, third commit (chuppatricky; open, not merged). Same bug class as
0084 (Lichii PR 100 and 65): the check that decides on shadow registers skips bits 32-39
unless the opcode is listed, and RED (0x98e) and SURED (0x59f) were not. A data register
in the reserved range then read the lowering's own uniform mirror instead of the guest
value, with no error.

Added here, unlike the PR: PrepareRegisterPressure's own cases. Lichii already has them
in register_pressure.h; ours had neither, so the check alone would have rejected those
programs with "native program uses lowering scratch registers". Operands copied from
Lichii's table at f356d39ba. A RED or SURED whose address register was reserved failed
with that same error before and now lowers.

Lichii could not tie this to a visible symptom in Ocarina either.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
index dfccd7d..12161ad 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
@@ -97,6 +97,11 @@ inline RegisterPressure PrepareRegisterPressure(const Instruction& input, u32 re
     case 0x321: operand(16, input.Bits(74, 2) + 1); operand(24); operand(32); break;
     case 0x322: operand(24); operand(32, input.Bits(74, 2) + 1); break;
     case 0x927: operand(24); operand(32); break;
+    case 0x59f: operand(24, 2); operand(32); break;
+    case 0x98e:
+        operand(24, input.Bits(72, 1) ? 2 : 1);
+        operand(32, input.Bits(73, 3) == 2 || input.Bits(73, 3) == 5 ? 2 : 1);
+        break;
     case 0x202: case 0x243: operand(16); operand(32); break;
     case 0x812: case 0x824: case 0x831: case 0x424: case 0x624:
         operand(16); operand(24); operand(64); break;
@@ -265,7 +270,8 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
         bool requires_shadow = false;
         for (u32 bit : {16U, 24U, 32U, 64U}) {
             if (bit == 32 && insn.Bits(9, 3) != 1 && opcode != 0xb60 && opcode != 0xb66 && opcode != 0xf66 &&
-                opcode != 0x988 && opcode != 0x986 && opcode != 0x927) continue;
+                opcode != 0x988 && opcode != 0x986 && opcode != 0x927 && opcode != 0x98e &&
+                opcode != 0x59f) continue;
             const u32 reg = insn.Bits(bit, 8);
             if (reg >= shadow_boundary && reg < 255) requires_shadow = true;
         }
